1
00:00:08,788 --> 00:00:11,908
That piercing noise...

2
00:00:35,328 --> 00:00:36,728
What is this place?

3
00:00:39,228 --> 00:00:40,868
An amusement park?

4
00:00:42,088 --> 00:00:43,808
I've never been here before.

5
00:00:45,608 --> 00:00:49,196
Why in the world am I riding on
a Ferris wheel in my pajamas?

6
00:00:49,748 --> 00:00:51,028
How'd I get here?

7
00:00:51,868 --> 00:00:52,808
The desert.

8
00:00:53,188 --> 00:00:57,482
I remember being in the desert, riding
through Saudi Arabia on camelback.

9
00:00:57,728 --> 00:00:59,199
But where are the others?

10
00:01:00,988 --> 00:01:02,488
Did they abandon me?

11
00:01:08,488 --> 00:01:10,135
This isn't making any sense.

12
00:01:10,368 --> 00:01:12,945
There's not a soul anywhere
in the amusement park.

13
00:01:13,028 --> 00:01:15,204
So why do I hear the cries of a baby?

14
00:01:15,568 --> 00:01:17,509
And for that matter, where is it?

15
00:01:34,028 --> 00:01:36,585
This card is...

16
00:01:36,668 --> 00:01:38,088
Death 13!

17
00:01:39,948 --> 00:01:42,368
Oh no, the card is moving!

18
00:01:58,768 --> 00:01:59,598
Kaku-ing!

19
00:02:01,528 --> 00:02:02,685
Kaku-ing! Kaku-ing!

20
00:02:02,768 --> 00:02:04,248
Hey, take it easy.

21
00:02:04,508 --> 00:02:08,245
Stop screaming and shaking the bed like
that creepy girl from The Exorcist.

22
00:02:08,328 --> 00:02:09,645
You're weirding me out.

23
00:02:09,728 --> 00:02:10,605
Where are we?

24
00:02:10,688 --> 00:02:12,548
Don't ask stupid questions.

25
00:02:13,188 --> 00:02:15,600
Now come on and get up already, would ya?

26
00:02:20,228 --> 00:02:22,993
After breakfast, we're
gonna take to the skies.

27
00:02:23,868 --> 00:02:25,868
Looks like another scorcher today.

28
00:02:27,108 --> 00:02:28,908
I had a terrible nightmare.

29
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,868
It was truly horrifying.

30
00:02:32,428 --> 00:02:33,588
You don't say.

31
00:02:33,928 --> 00:02:35,005
Lay on the details.

32
00:02:35,088 --> 00:02:36,928
I want to hear all about it.

33
00:02:37,268 --> 00:02:39,105
Well, the thing is, I can't remember.

34
00:02:39,188 --> 00:02:40,205
I've forgotten it all.

35
00:02:40,288 --> 00:02:41,118
Come again?

36
00:02:41,748 --> 00:02:43,513
Regardless, it was petrifying.

37
00:02:44,248 --> 00:02:47,130
But when you woke me up,
you pulled me out of it.

38
00:02:47,308 --> 00:02:51,132
Wish we could talk more about it,
but we've got to get a move on.

39
00:02:52,228 --> 00:02:53,058
Let's go.

40
00:02:53,141 --> 00:02:54,341
Hurry up and get ready.

41
00:03:00,408 --> 00:03:01,879
There's a cut on my hand.

42
00:03:03,508 --> 00:03:04,908
But how'd it get there?

43
00:03:21,948 --> 00:03:27,145
And now I'm going to be a star dust?

44
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:33,965
A hundred years ago, I'm
called to be a star dust.

45
00:03:34,048 --> 00:03:39,465
The men are going towards the

46
00:03:39,548 --> 00:03:43,108
end of the tunnel of the time.

47
00:03:47,768 --> 00:03:49,808
It's like a karma.

48
00:03:52,048 --> 00:03:54,328
It's a destiny.

49
00:04:39,108 --> 00:04:40,108
Jotaro and Mr.

50
00:04:40,228 --> 00:04:43,225
Joestar are already headed to the
plane, so we'll meet them there.

51
00:04:43,308 --> 00:04:46,837
And the way I hear it, we're
traveling 500 kilometers today.

52
00:04:47,968 --> 00:04:48,798
No!

53
00:04:48,881 --> 00:04:49,711
This can't be happening!

54
00:04:49,868 --> 00:04:51,748
Please stop, my poor dog!

55
00:04:52,768 --> 00:04:54,548
My dog is dead!

56
00:04:56,508 --> 00:04:59,588
Who would do such a thing? A dog?

57
00:05:00,888 --> 00:05:01,718
Dog?

58
00:05:02,408 --> 00:05:06,348
I could have sworn that I saw
a dead dog not too long ago.

59
00:05:06,588 --> 00:05:10,005
Whoever did this is sick, but
there's nothing we can do about it.

60
00:05:10,088 --> 00:05:10,918
Let's go.

61
00:05:13,928 --> 00:05:15,548
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

62
00:05:15,888 --> 00:05:17,288
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

63
00:05:17,468 --> 00:05:19,586
Hold on a dang second there, mister!

64
00:05:20,308 --> 00:05:23,668
What exactly do you mean you
can't sell us the plane now?

65
00:05:23,968 --> 00:05:28,245
I seem to recall you taking my money
last night and saying it was a done deal.

66
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:32,065
You'll get a full refund, but first
we need to see to a baby with a fever.

67
00:05:32,148 --> 00:05:34,488
It's 39 degrees Celsius. Huh?

68
00:05:34,868 --> 00:05:36,265
There's no doctor in this town,

69
00:05:36,348 --> 00:05:40,407
so we have no choice but to take
the baby somewhere else to get help.

70
00:05:43,068 --> 00:05:45,965
Okay, then, what do you say to
us taking that plane over there?

71
00:05:46,048 --> 00:05:47,685
I'm sorry to say that one's broken.

72
00:05:47,768 --> 00:05:48,608
What's up?

73
00:05:48,828 --> 00:05:49,985
Some kind of argument?

74
00:05:50,068 --> 00:05:50,898
Yeah.

75
00:05:51,368 --> 00:05:52,198
A baby?

76
00:05:53,568 --> 00:05:54,608
A baby.

77
00:05:55,768 --> 00:05:57,888
I remember hearing a baby's cries.

78
00:05:59,768 --> 00:06:00,648
But where?

79
00:06:01,728 --> 00:06:04,885
You'll be able to use the plane
after it gets back tomorrow night.

80
00:06:04,968 --> 00:06:07,321
We can renegotiate and talk prices then.

81
00:06:07,428 --> 00:06:09,016
Did you say tomorrow night?

82
00:06:09,188 --> 00:06:12,485
Our group has someone's life on
the line just like you guys do.

83
00:06:12,568 --> 00:06:15,365
We can't afford to spend two
days pissing around this place.

84
00:06:15,448 --> 00:06:19,036
So, what you're telling me is
you'd rather let that baby die?

85
00:06:21,248 --> 00:06:22,205
Well, I...

86
00:06:22,288 --> 00:06:24,648
Excuse me, I have a suggestion.

87
00:06:24,928 --> 00:06:27,605
We can kill two birds
with one stone by having

88
00:06:27,688 --> 00:06:30,570
these gentlemen taken to
the doctor on their way.

89
00:06:31,288 --> 00:06:32,685
Nice idea, but...

90
00:06:32,768 --> 00:06:37,297
The Cessna is built to carry four, but
surely there's enough room for a baby.

91
00:06:39,428 --> 00:06:41,722
I could have sworn I just saw it smile.

92
00:06:42,108 --> 00:06:44,284
And that the child already has teeth.

93
00:06:44,968 --> 00:06:46,497
You sure about this, lady?

94
00:06:46,648 --> 00:06:49,205
Do you really want to leave
your baby with these guys?

95
00:06:49,288 --> 00:06:50,265
Uh, just a minute.

96
00:06:50,348 --> 00:06:51,505
We can't do that either.

97
00:06:51,588 --> 00:06:54,412
It's too dangerous for
the baby to come with us.

98
00:07:00,748 --> 00:07:02,807
I told him this would be dangerous.

99
00:07:03,108 --> 00:07:04,985
Hey, just try and take it easy, Mr.

100
00:07:05,068 --> 00:07:05,898
Joestar.

101
00:07:05,981 --> 00:07:09,985
There's no way a stand could catch a plane
flying hundreds of kilometers an hour.

102
00:07:10,068 --> 00:07:12,945
I mean, we even made sure the
plane itself wasn't a stand.

103
00:07:13,028 --> 00:07:14,499
I'd say we're good to go.

104
00:07:14,648 --> 00:07:16,665
I'm far more worried about the old man's

105
00:07:16,748 --> 00:07:19,395
flying than I am in
attack from enemy stands.

106
00:07:35,228 --> 00:07:36,608
Oh, thank goodness.

107
00:07:37,088 --> 00:07:37,968
What a relief.

108
00:07:39,448 --> 00:07:43,048
By the way, I wonder who
that baby belonged to. Huh?

109
00:07:43,368 --> 00:07:45,845
Are you saying you're not the
mother of that child, miss?

110
00:07:45,928 --> 00:07:46,758
Oh, no.

111
00:07:46,841 --> 00:07:48,605
I found it by the well this morning.

112
00:07:48,688 --> 00:07:53,448
Though, from the moment I heard the babies
crying, I wasn't able to help myself.

113
00:07:53,688 --> 00:07:55,988
I felt I had to put him on that plane.

114
00:07:56,808 --> 00:07:57,867
What could happen?

115
00:08:10,768 --> 00:08:14,768
Maybe it's just me, but I always
get so tired when I get on a plane.

116
00:08:15,048 --> 00:08:16,505
If it's all right with you, Mr.

117
00:08:16,588 --> 00:08:19,565
Joestar, I think I'm going
to take a Monday catnap.

118
00:08:19,648 --> 00:08:20,478
Sure!

119
00:08:31,188 --> 00:08:32,588
What is this?

120
00:08:33,128 --> 00:08:36,968
Hey, Kakyoin, where the hell
are we? Where'd Mr. Joestar go?

121
00:08:38,488 --> 00:08:40,959
This is the same dream I had this morning.

122
00:08:41,068 --> 00:08:43,715
But now it seems we're
both inside the dream.

123
00:08:44,048 --> 00:08:46,108
What? A dream? Yes.

124
00:08:47,768 --> 00:08:48,605
That's a relief.

125
00:08:48,688 --> 00:08:50,159
It's just a stupid dream.

126
00:08:50,528 --> 00:08:52,208
I was worried for a second.

127
00:08:52,388 --> 00:08:55,623
But if it's only a dream,
who cares if the dog is dead?

128
00:08:55,808 --> 00:08:57,690
Polnareff, you can't be serious.

129
00:08:58,228 --> 00:09:00,585
Dreams are only as scary as you make them.

130
00:09:00,668 --> 00:09:02,492
That's kind of the way it goes.

131
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:04,188
Oh, just try and relax.

132
00:09:04,568 --> 00:09:07,185
How can I relax when we're
having the same dream?

133
00:09:07,268 --> 00:09:09,209
I suppose you have a point there.

134
00:09:09,488 --> 00:09:10,908
This is kind of weird.

135
00:09:11,228 --> 00:09:13,581
But in a dream, isn't anything possible?

136
00:09:13,928 --> 00:09:15,848
Oh, boy, would you look at that!

137
00:09:15,968 --> 00:09:17,674
This dreaming thing is great!

138
00:09:18,128 --> 00:09:19,088
So good!

139
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,098
See?

140
00:09:21,181 --> 00:09:24,773
All you have to do to make your
dreams fun is think they're fun.

141
00:09:25,408 --> 00:09:28,685
Listen, do you remember seeing
the dog's carcass this morning?

142
00:09:28,768 --> 00:09:30,765
Obviously, the dog and
I had the same dream,

143
00:09:30,848 --> 00:09:33,965
and in that dream, that dog
was unmistakably slaughtered.

144
00:09:34,048 --> 00:09:36,868
Once I was awake, I found
this cut on my hand.

145
00:09:37,608 --> 00:09:38,438
Where from?

146
00:09:39,188 --> 00:09:41,388
From the enemy's stand. Death 13.

147
00:09:42,068 --> 00:09:44,108
The enemy's stand. Mm-hmm.

148
00:09:45,088 --> 00:09:46,748
Oh, I get it now.

149
00:09:46,948 --> 00:09:49,485
You're paranoid because you
had a dream about stands.

150
00:09:49,568 --> 00:09:51,465
Man, you have got to take it easy.

151
00:09:51,548 --> 00:09:52,378
You're wrong.

152
00:09:52,461 --> 00:09:53,808
It wasn't a dream about stands.

153
00:09:54,188 --> 00:09:55,465
A stand was in my dream.

154
00:09:55,548 --> 00:09:58,725
That's what I said, you were
having a dream about stands.

155
00:09:58,808 --> 00:10:00,867
Ah, you still don't get it, do you?

156
00:10:01,528 --> 00:10:02,358
Loli-ho!

157
00:10:02,648 --> 00:10:05,188
Tell me, does it hurt being that stupid?

158
00:10:10,388 --> 00:10:13,348
Oh, for the love of, let
me spell it out for you.

159
00:10:13,508 --> 00:10:16,626
I'm saying that you're slow
on the uptake, palmer-up.

160
00:10:17,028 --> 00:10:18,969
It's coming from the dog's wound.

161
00:10:22,148 --> 00:10:23,048
Lo-de-ho!

162
00:10:23,368 --> 00:10:25,785
Allow me to welcome
you to my humble abode!

163
00:10:25,868 --> 00:10:27,825
This is a dream, and I'm the Grand Reaper!

164
00:10:27,908 --> 00:10:29,008
It's a megaphone?

165
00:10:37,808 --> 00:10:38,638
What the...

166
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:39,746
what is that thing?

167
00:10:39,948 --> 00:10:42,025
Polnareff, stay on
guard and watch closely.

168
00:10:42,108 --> 00:10:43,461
That fiend is Death 13!

169
00:10:54,088 --> 00:10:56,048
Come forth, Hierophant Green!

170
00:10:58,508 --> 00:10:59,628
Hierophant, attack!

171
00:11:01,268 --> 00:11:02,098
Giorno!

172
00:11:03,788 --> 00:11:06,008
Why can't I summon Hierophant?

173
00:11:06,148 --> 00:11:07,008
What is this?

174
00:11:07,308 --> 00:11:09,588
I can't get my stand to appear either!

175
00:11:10,448 --> 00:11:14,488
Is it because we're in some
kind of twisted dream? Alley-ho!

176
00:11:14,988 --> 00:11:16,988
It's romantic, wouldn't you agree?

177
00:11:17,148 --> 00:11:18,968
Being able to die in a dream?

178
00:11:20,268 --> 00:11:21,288
Alley-ho!

179
00:11:38,828 --> 00:11:40,488
Jotaro, do you sense that?

180
00:11:41,888 --> 00:11:43,328
Yeah, clear as day.

181
00:11:49,788 --> 00:11:51,508
Are you stupid?

182
00:11:51,848 --> 00:11:55,377
Surely you know by now that
only a stand can defeat a stand.

183
00:11:55,528 --> 00:11:59,648
It's time for you to enter
your eternal sleep, Pone Ref.

184
00:12:01,708 --> 00:12:02,608
Alley-o!

185
00:12:03,288 --> 00:12:04,608
Pull the ref! Die!

186
00:12:10,328 --> 00:12:11,268
Pull the ref.

187
00:12:12,848 --> 00:12:14,488
Hey, Polnareff, wake up!

188
00:12:15,248 --> 00:12:18,307
It would appear our little
traveler has wet himself.

189
00:12:18,428 --> 00:12:20,781
Do us all a favor and change his diaper.

190
00:12:25,708 --> 00:12:26,538
Curses!

191
00:12:26,621 --> 00:12:29,085
Someone must have woken
the fool from his slumber.

192
00:12:29,168 --> 00:12:30,828
He's quite lucky.

193
00:12:32,868 --> 00:12:35,108
Lollyho, I suppose it's no matter.

194
00:12:35,348 --> 00:12:38,105
Even if he wakes up, he won't
remember a single thing.

195
00:12:38,188 --> 00:12:41,848
I'll just have to finish him
the next time he falls asleep.

196
00:12:43,188 --> 00:12:46,428
Which means your death has been moved up.

197
00:12:48,208 --> 00:12:49,038
Lollyho!

198
00:12:49,308 --> 00:12:50,808
Hey there, Polnareff.

199
00:12:50,968 --> 00:12:52,165
Have you woken up yet?

200
00:12:52,248 --> 00:12:54,408
I like that diaper change this year.

201
00:12:54,568 --> 00:12:56,128
All right, I'm up, I'm up.

202
00:12:57,988 --> 00:13:01,748
Man, I feel like I had some
kind of terrifying nightmare.

203
00:13:02,168 --> 00:13:04,908
But I don't remember what happened at all.

204
00:13:05,088 --> 00:13:06,525
I've completely forgotten.

205
00:13:06,608 --> 00:13:08,728
After you change the boy's diaper,

206
00:13:09,028 --> 00:13:11,465
you can head back to dreamland
to finish your business.

207
00:13:11,548 --> 00:13:13,019
I won't wake you up again

208
00:13:17,888 --> 00:13:19,708
Mad hold on a second guys.

209
00:13:19,928 --> 00:13:23,248
What the hell is this the kid
took a dump in his diaper.

210
00:13:23,508 --> 00:13:26,688
Just look at the size of
it Well, he is a baby.

211
00:13:26,868 --> 00:13:28,905
You know, that's why he wears diapers.

212
00:13:28,988 --> 00:13:29,965
You're kidding me.

213
00:13:30,048 --> 00:13:30,878
That's why

214
00:13:32,968 --> 00:13:33,798
Say, Douglas.

215
00:13:33,881 --> 00:13:35,729
What a vile, disgusting creature.

216
00:13:35,948 --> 00:13:37,945
And he's gotten it all over the place.

217
00:13:38,028 --> 00:13:40,765
Would you stop yapping and
change the damn diaper already?

218
00:13:40,848 --> 00:13:41,678
It stinks.

219
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:45,595
How are you not embarrassed?

220
00:13:45,968 --> 00:13:48,208
Do us all a favor and grow up already.

221
00:13:51,128 --> 00:13:52,585
Does this look right to you?

222
00:13:52,668 --> 00:13:54,268
Well, it looks good to me.

223
00:13:54,568 --> 00:13:56,725
Jotaro, I need you to
hold on to the edge there.

224
00:13:56,808 --> 00:13:58,288
I'm gonna try and pin it.

225
00:13:59,208 --> 00:14:00,285
Okay. Like this?

226
00:14:00,368 --> 00:14:01,648
Yeah, I think so.

227
00:14:01,788 --> 00:14:03,348
Now hold on to the baby.

228
00:14:18,628 --> 00:14:19,458
Stop it!

229
00:14:19,541 --> 00:14:21,428
Kick, what's wrong? Hey!

230
00:14:28,168 --> 00:14:29,068
Damn it!

231
00:14:31,508 --> 00:14:32,788
I've lost control!

232
00:14:33,328 --> 00:14:36,928
Wait, are you saying that
we're going to crash? Stop!

233
00:14:37,308 --> 00:14:39,426
Kakyoin, what's the matter with you?

234
00:14:39,748 --> 00:14:41,866
He's been this way since he woke up!

235
00:14:42,088 --> 00:14:44,288
I don't care, just calm him down!

236
00:14:44,928 --> 00:14:49,104
Old man, if you don't regain control
of this thing, we're all done for!

237
00:14:52,368 --> 00:14:55,468
Kakyoin, you need to pull
yourself together pronto!

238
00:14:55,888 --> 00:14:58,006
We're about to crash because of you!

239
00:14:58,908 --> 00:14:59,738
Lally-ho!

240
00:15:00,428 --> 00:15:02,185
Talk about a restless sleeper.

241
00:15:02,268 --> 00:15:03,745
At this rate, you'll kill us both.

242
00:15:03,828 --> 00:15:05,368
You and my user, that is.

243
00:15:06,428 --> 00:15:07,868
Your user is that baby?

244
00:15:08,108 --> 00:15:10,108
How in the world is that possible?

245
00:15:11,708 --> 00:15:12,538
No way.

246
00:15:12,908 --> 00:15:14,968
He's only about six months old.

247
00:15:15,888 --> 00:15:16,718
Wrong!

248
00:15:16,801 --> 00:15:18,828
I'm 11 months, almost a year old.

249
00:15:19,108 --> 00:15:21,765
It may also interest you
to know that I'm a genius.

250
00:15:21,848 --> 00:15:26,142
I may poop in my diapers, but I know
a hell of a lot more than you fools.

251
00:15:32,608 --> 00:15:33,438
Yaaaaaah!

252
00:15:41,228 --> 00:15:45,268
And with that, you've lost
your ability to scream.

253
00:15:46,528 --> 00:15:48,188
A stand within a dream.

254
00:15:48,488 --> 00:15:50,968
I have to find a way to let Mr.

255
00:15:51,088 --> 00:15:52,568
Joestar and Jotaro know.

256
00:15:55,628 --> 00:15:56,458
Hm?

257
00:15:56,541 --> 00:15:57,781
What are you doing, Mr.

258
00:15:57,868 --> 00:15:58,698
Joespawn?

259
00:15:58,781 --> 00:15:59,611
Damn it, level us out!

260
00:15:59,694 --> 00:16:00,524
Just calm down!

261
00:16:00,607 --> 00:16:04,821
Can't you see I'm working on that while
trying to stay cool and collected?

262
00:16:05,828 --> 00:16:07,128
I'm not waking up!

263
00:16:07,708 --> 00:16:08,538
Lally-ho!

264
00:16:09,028 --> 00:16:11,385
Looks to me like no one's going
to notice if you're cutting

265
00:16:11,468 --> 00:16:14,586
your arm with a knife that's
smaller than my wee-wee!

266
00:16:15,728 --> 00:16:20,345
Besides, you can hurt yourself all you want
in this dream, but it won't wake you up!

267
00:16:20,428 --> 00:16:25,828
As long as you're asleep, I completely
control every iota of your precious mind.

268
00:16:26,308 --> 00:16:28,308
My stand, Death 13,

269
00:16:28,648 --> 00:16:30,545
infiltrates the minds of its slumbering

270
00:16:30,628 --> 00:16:33,393
victims when they are at
their most vulnerable.

271
00:16:34,828 --> 00:16:36,708
Dammit! Stop!

272
00:16:40,548 --> 00:16:42,168
What's wrong, old man?

273
00:16:42,468 --> 00:16:43,488
We're crashing!

274
00:16:44,668 --> 00:16:46,968
I'll control it with Hermit Purple!

275
00:16:52,028 --> 00:16:52,908
I did it!

276
00:16:53,128 --> 00:16:55,828
I lifted the plane just
in the nick of time!

277
00:16:56,128 --> 00:16:57,508
What a close one!

278
00:16:58,808 --> 00:17:01,648
It would seem we managed
to avoid crashing.

279
00:17:01,948 --> 00:17:03,772
That was too close for comfort.

280
00:17:05,128 --> 00:17:10,348
Now then, what do you see to me killing
you by crushing that heart of yours?

281
00:17:10,688 --> 00:17:11,518
That way,

282
00:17:11,601 --> 00:17:16,389
Joestar and the others will think you had
a heart attack and died of natural causes.

283
00:17:17,748 --> 00:17:18,828
Die, Cuckooine!

284
00:17:19,168 --> 00:17:20,525
Did you guys see that?

285
00:17:20,608 --> 00:17:22,549
How do you boys like them apples?

286
00:17:22,828 --> 00:17:24,428
My flying's not too shabby!

287
00:17:29,488 --> 00:17:30,318
What?

288
00:17:30,428 --> 00:17:33,505
Why the hell is there a palm
tree all the way out here?

289
00:17:33,588 --> 00:17:35,348
Good grief. Damn.

290
00:17:36,908 --> 00:17:38,688
I knew you'd do this!

291
00:17:56,968 --> 00:17:58,728
Is this enough, Mr. Joestar?

292
00:17:59,408 --> 00:18:00,768
Yeah, thank you.

293
00:18:02,708 --> 00:18:04,248
We survived, butt.

294
00:18:05,208 --> 00:18:07,328
Kakyoin, what's going on, man?

295
00:18:07,528 --> 00:18:09,469
This is all your fault, you know.

296
00:18:10,688 --> 00:18:11,828
I'm not sure.

297
00:18:12,708 --> 00:18:15,548
I feel like I just
endured a horrible dream.

298
00:18:15,828 --> 00:18:18,708
And when I awoke, I was utterly exhausted.

299
00:18:19,448 --> 00:18:22,268
I think there's something wrong with me.

300
00:18:22,428 --> 00:18:23,668
Try and cheer up.

301
00:18:23,848 --> 00:18:25,730
It's probably a case of fatigue.

302
00:18:26,048 --> 00:18:28,685
It's been about a month
now since we left Japan.

303
00:18:28,768 --> 00:18:32,474
And the enemy's been attacking
us non-stop ever since that day.

304
00:18:32,928 --> 00:18:33,758
Hey.

305
00:18:33,841 --> 00:18:36,865
It looks like the baby's
fever has finally gone down.

306
00:18:36,948 --> 00:18:38,845
Thank goodness he's safe and sound.

307
00:18:38,928 --> 00:18:42,645
If anything were to happen to this
little guy, I'd never forgive myself.

308
00:18:42,728 --> 00:18:43,558
Ah!

309
00:18:45,888 --> 00:18:46,808
Peek-a-boo!

310
00:18:47,448 --> 00:18:48,278
Blah!

311
00:18:49,648 --> 00:18:50,648
Peek-a-boo!

312
00:18:52,468 --> 00:18:55,608
He has such an adorable
smile, don't you think?

313
00:18:55,828 --> 00:18:57,805
I really don't get what's so funny.

314
00:18:57,888 --> 00:19:00,535
You're not even making
any jokes, just faces.

315
00:19:00,688 --> 00:19:01,648
What an idiot.

316
00:19:03,508 --> 00:19:05,288
Oh, put a sock in it.

317
00:19:05,408 --> 00:19:08,148
This isn't my idea of
a perfect night either.

318
00:19:08,908 --> 00:19:11,308
Hey, old man, the radio survived.

319
00:19:11,728 --> 00:19:12,787
What should we do?

320
00:19:12,948 --> 00:19:15,028
Should we send out an SOS?

321
00:19:15,568 --> 00:19:18,788
That'll mean Dio can find
us, but... We have to.

322
00:19:19,088 --> 00:19:21,735
Let's call for a rescue,
for the baby's sake.

323
00:19:25,968 --> 00:19:26,798
Huh?

324
00:19:26,881 --> 00:19:29,888
I thought I was feeling
twinches of pain. I'm bleeding.

325
00:19:31,248 --> 00:19:33,307
Wait, did I cut it when we crashed?

326
00:19:42,588 --> 00:19:43,418
What's this?

327
00:19:43,648 --> 00:19:44,988
The cuts form letters.

328
00:19:45,948 --> 00:19:50,925
Baby stand but how did they I don't
know what it means even though it's

329
00:19:51,008 --> 00:19:53,545
my handwriting I can't remember

330
00:19:53,628 --> 00:20:00,545
anything did I do this to myself there

331
00:20:00,628 --> 00:20:04,665
isn't any blood on my knife but it
seems the cuts were made with this blade

332
00:20:04,748 --> 00:20:10,008
wait a minute could I have really
forgotten violently cutting my own arm?

333
00:20:14,288 --> 00:20:15,118
Damn it!

334
00:20:15,388 --> 00:20:16,968
I was told he was clever,

335
00:20:18,468 --> 00:20:21,605
but I never thought he'd actually
carve letters into his arm?

336
00:20:21,688 --> 00:20:23,570
while trying to wake himself up.

337
00:20:27,368 --> 00:20:30,133
What was that look on
the baby's face just now?

338
00:20:30,668 --> 00:20:34,492
It's as if he deliberately looked
away the moment I met his gaze.

339
00:20:37,588 --> 00:20:38,418
Baby.

340
00:20:39,168 --> 00:20:39,998
Baby, stand.

341
00:20:45,988 --> 00:20:47,228
Baby, stand.

342
00:20:53,128 --> 00:20:57,888
I hate to say it, but I might
be losing my mind, because...

343
00:20:59,328 --> 00:21:01,768
I'm starting to think...

344
00:21:03,168 --> 00:21:05,768
that this baby is a stand user!

345
00:21:08,808 --> 00:21:11,628
Hey, Kakyoin, what do
you think you're doing?

346
00:21:13,228 --> 00:21:14,248
Come on, now.

347
00:21:14,568 --> 00:21:15,862
That is way too rough.

348
00:21:16,088 --> 00:21:17,559
You can strangle the boy.

349
00:21:17,688 --> 00:21:18,805
What's wrong with you?

350
00:21:18,888 --> 00:21:19,908
My apologies.

351
00:21:21,148 --> 00:21:21,978
There, there.

352
00:21:22,061 --> 00:21:23,381
Everything's all right.

353
00:21:23,608 --> 00:21:25,625
Let's have something to eat, shall we?

354
00:21:25,708 --> 00:21:28,590
He should calm down once
he has some food in him.

355
00:21:29,888 --> 00:21:31,028
Hey, Jotaro.

356
00:21:31,368 --> 00:21:35,192
It looks like poor Kakyoin's really
starting to lose it out here.

357
00:21:35,448 --> 00:21:36,945
Hmm. There, there.

358
00:21:37,028 --> 00:21:40,322
I wonder if he'll make it
through the rest of this trip.

359
00:22:11,688 --> 00:22:14,365
All the old paintings on the tomb.

360
00:22:14,448 --> 00:22:16,405
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

361
00:22:16,488 --> 00:22:18,048
If they move too quick!

362
00:22:18,708 --> 00:22:21,105
They're falling down like a domino.

363
00:22:21,188 --> 00:22:23,725
All the birds are men by the Nile.

364
00:22:23,808 --> 00:22:27,385
They got their money on
a bed Called crocodiles.

365
00:22:27,468 --> 00:22:30,365
They snap their teeth on your cigarette.

366
00:22:30,448 --> 00:22:32,768
Falling tight to the hookah? I say,

367
00:22:32,928 --> 00:22:33,758
walk

368
00:22:33,841 --> 00:22:40,725
like

369
00:22:40,808 --> 00:22:41,638
an Egyptian.

370
00:22:53,428 --> 00:22:58,345
The blonde waitresses take their trays,
spin around and they cross the floor.

371
00:22:58,428 --> 00:22:59,845
They've got the moves.

372
00:22:59,928 --> 00:23:01,825
You drop your drink.

373
00:23:01,908 --> 00:23:03,025
Then they bring you more.

374
00:23:03,108 --> 00:23:04,145
All the school kids.

375
00:23:04,228 --> 00:23:05,645
So sick of books?

376
00:23:05,728 --> 00:23:06,558
They're like the punk.

377
00:23:06,641 --> 00:23:07,705
And the metal band.

378
00:23:07,788 --> 00:23:09,268
When the buzzer rings.

379
00:23:09,968 --> 00:23:10,865
They're walking.

380
00:23:10,948 --> 00:23:11,965
Like an Egyptian.

381
00:23:12,048 --> 00:23:14,005
All the kids. In the marketplace.

382
00:23:14,088 --> 00:23:15,085
Walk

383
00:23:15,168 --> 00:23:22,168
like

384
00:23:22,788 --> 00:23:23,618
an Egyptian.

385
00:23:29,368 --> 00:23:30,365
Did you see that?

386
00:23:30,448 --> 00:23:31,645
Knock it off, Cockyween.

387
00:23:31,728 --> 00:23:32,558
That's enough.

388
00:23:32,641 --> 00:23:33,545
How stupid can you be?

389
00:23:33,628 --> 00:23:35,205
But I'm sure that he's a stand user!

390
00:23:35,288 --> 00:23:37,225
You didn't do that to yourself, did you?

391
00:23:37,308 --> 00:23:38,145
What's going on?

392
00:23:38,228 --> 00:23:39,605
Did I make things even worse?

393
00:23:39,688 --> 00:23:40,828
Not at all!
